  "prefLabel": "Ed 1021.06 Scheduling of Mediation, Prehearing Conference, and Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1021.06 Scheduling of Mediation, Prehearing Conference, and Hearing.\n\n(a) At the time of the filing of a request to initiate a hearing under Ed 1021.07, the parties shall notify the office of legislation and hearings in the designated state agency of whether they wish to pursue mediation prior to a prehearing conference and a hearing.\n\n(b) If the parties choose not to engage in mediation, the office of legislation and hearings in the department of education shall schedule the prehearing conference and hearing based on hearing officer availability, as provided in Ed 1021.10.\n\n(c) The scheduling shall allow for the following:\n\n(1) A day for an alternative dispute resolution, if the parties so decide;\n\n(2) A half day for a prehearing conference; and\n\n(3) A minimum of 2 days for a hearing.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Ed 1000) #13231, eff 7-13-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1000.html"
